cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: 'Chess-MHSUC — Human Chess Under Clock Constraints: A Replication and Benchmark Study'
abstract: A reproducible replication and benchmark study of human move quality and clock constraints in online chess, covering 145,000+ Lichess games and 8.3M+ move-level observations across three time controls (3+0, 5+0, 10+0) and two independent monthly samples. The study decomposes the clock-related final-outcome signal into a mechanical time-forfeit channel and a board-decided channel, and compares it with next-move quality among board-decided games. Results are predictive and descriptive, not causal.
